# Hostlinks Zoom — Git commits and GitHub releases

Use this whenever you ship changes to **this repository**. The in-plugin auto-updater reads **GitHub Releases** (`releases/latest`) and the release asset **`hostlinks-zoom.zip`**.

## Repository root

This directory is the Git repo root (`hostlinks-zoom.php`, `.github/workflows/`, etc.).

- Remote: `https://github.com/spkldbrd/hostlinks-zoom`
- Default branch: `main`

Run **git** and manual **zip** steps from here (or `git -C <path>`).

---

## Step 1 — Bump the version

Edit **both** places in `hostlinks-zoom.php`:

```php
 * Version:     1.0.0
...
define( 'HLZ_VERSION', '1.0.0' );
```

Bump **`HLZ_DB_VERSION`** only when the database schema changes.

---

## Step 2 — Commit and push (PowerShell)

**Do not use `&&` or bash heredocs** — use separate lines or `;` in PowerShell.

```powershell
Set-Location "c:\cursor\Hostlinks 2.0\wp-content\plugins\hostlinks-zoom"
$msg = "fix: short description (v1.X.X)"
git add -A
git commit -m $msg
git push origin main
```

Prefer **Conventional Commits** (`fix:`, `feat:`, `ci:`, `docs:`) and mention the version when useful.

---

## Step 3 — Release zip (default: GitHub Actions)

A push to **`main`** runs [`.github/workflows/release-zip.yml`](.github/workflows/release-zip.yml):

1. Parses **`HLZ_VERSION`** from `hostlinks-zoom.php`.
2. Builds **`hostlinks-zoom.zip`** with top-level folder **`hostlinks-zoom/`** and Unix-style paths.
3. **Creates** a GitHub Release for that version if missing, or **`gh release upload --clobber`** to replace the zip on an existing release.

**Excluded from the zip:** `.git`, `.github`, `.cursor`, `build/`, stray `hostlinks-zoom.zip`.

Verify on GitHub: **Actions** job green, **Releases** shows the zip. Opening a Hostlinks Zoom admin screen clears the update cache.

**Agents:** after bumping the version, **always commit and push**. Do not stop before `git push` — that is what builds the auto-update.

---

## Step 4 — Manual zip + release (fallback)

If Actions is down. Use **.NET `ZipFile`**, not **`Compress-Archive`**, so entry names use **`/`**.

```powershell
$pluginDir = "c:\cursor\Hostlinks 2.0\wp-content\plugins\hostlinks-zoom"
$zipPath   = "c:\cursor\Hostlinks 2.0\wp-content\plugins\hostlinks-zoom.zip"
if (Test-Path $zipPath) { Remove-Item $zipPath -Force }
Add-Type -AssemblyName System.IO.Compression.FileSystem
$zip = [System.IO.Compression.ZipFile]::Open($zipPath, 'Create')
Get-ChildItem -Path $pluginDir -Recurse -File | Where-Object {
    $p = $_.FullName
    $p -notmatch '[\\/]\.git[\\/]' -and $p -notmatch '[\\/]\.github[\\/]' -and $p -notmatch '[\\/]\.cursor[\\/]'
} | ForEach-Object {
    $relative = $_.FullName.Substring($pluginDir.Length + 1).Replace('\', '/')
    $entry    = "hostlinks-zoom/$relative"
    [System.IO.Compression.ZipFileExtensions]::CreateEntryFromFile($zip, $_.FullName, $entry, 'Optimal') | Out-Null
}
$zip.Dispose()
```

```powershell
Set-Location "c:\cursor\Hostlinks 2.0\wp-content\plugins\hostlinks-zoom"
gh release create 1.X.X $zipPath --title "v1.X.X" --notes "…"
# gh release upload 1.X.X $zipPath --clobber
```

